  chapterText:
      'For nearly a century after archaeologists first excavated seals bearing the Indus Valley script from '
      'sites across the subcontinent, the writing system has stubbornly resisted every serious attempt at '
      'decipherment, remaining one of archaeology\'s most persistent unsolved puzzles despite the involvement '
